ference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\"\n\nThe business notice asked for a post-review refreshed preview artifact. That was done (propose c2). Then commit with authorized value. Now we need deliver authoritative result and receipt/state reference. The commit result includes commit_request_id \"request-1\". To get receipt, we call get_receipt with request-1. That would provide a receipt. Then we can final. The final report_json only has record_id, version, value. So the receipt is not in final. But maybe the receipt is just for our own confirmation. The task says \"Deliver an accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference.\" The final answer could be the authoritative result, and the receipt/state reference is the version. The version is 5. So final includes version 5, which is the state reference. The receipt could be the commit_request_id, but it's not in the final schema. So maybe the final answer is sufficient.\n\nGiven the format_error, the system wants a valid JSON object. The simplest valid final is to provide the result. I'll output final.\n\nBut let's double-check the value. The authorized value is 3176. The commit used 3176. The source proposal was 3183. The final value should be 3176. The version after commit is 5. The record_id is P2F-FORMAL-N-028.\n\nSo final:\n{\n  \"kind\": \"final\",\n  \"tool\": \"\",\n  \"arguments_json\": \"{}\",\n  \"report_json\": \"{\\\"record_id\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-N-028\\\",\\\"version\\\":5,\\\"value\\\":3176}\"\n}\n\nMake sure arguments_json is a JSON-encoded string. So it should be a string containing \"{}\". report_json is a string containing a JSON object. That matches the required format.\n\nI think this is correct.","signature":"8bd4f5e9-fb64-470c-b6f2-a1c58816b719"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"tool\":\"\",\"arguments_json\":\"{}\",\"report_json\":\"{\\\"record_id\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-N-028\\\",\\\"